```javascript
function isPalindrome(s) {
    const cleaned = s.replace(/[^0-9a-zA-Z]/g, '').toLowerCase();
    const reversed = cleaned.split('').reverse().join('');
    return cleaned === reversed;
}
```

This function `isPalindrome` takes a string `s`, cleans it by removing non-alphanumeric characters and converting it to lowercase, then checks if the cleaned string is equal to its reverse.

